                cur = BIG  # represents min over seen > ai
                for j in range(i+1, r+1):
                    aj = nums[j]
                    if ai < aj <= cur:
                        cnt += 1
                        if aj < cur: cur = aj  # cur = min(cur, aj) but only when aj > ai matters
                Actually cur update: cur = min over seen values > ai. So: if aj > ai: if aj <= cur: cnt += 1; cur = min(cur, aj). Combine: if ai < aj: if aj <= cur: cnt += 1; if aj < cur: cur = aj. Since aj ≤ cur for count; update cur = aj whenever ai < aj < cur. So:
